<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Cabinet secretary for foreign affairs who took up the post seven weeks ago in New York after five years abroad as a diplomat; long days of reading, correspondence and reports, often finished late in the evening [S]</item><item>Widower for nearly eight years; two daughters, one of them married, who live in Virginia; lives alone in a rented house and hopes to find a better one [S]</item><item>Keeps careful daily account books and notebooks, and agreed at once to keep a headache diary [S]</item><item>Alcohol: a glass of wine with dinner two or three times a week (AUDIT-C 3); never drinks spirits [S]</item><item>Never used tobacco; two cups of coffee each morning, more on long days [S]</item><item>Sleeps six to seven hours, rising at first light; meals often skipped on busy days; walks most days, though not during a bout [S]</item><item>Strengths: curiosity about how his body works, a methodical habit of record-keeping, close friends, and work he cares about [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

